ory label> \nPriority 4 = Global Pulse News branding> \nPriority 5 = Date/supporting information> \n> \nTEXT LIMIT:> \n- Total text on the image should normally stay below 20 words.> \n- Never put the full article on the image.> \n- Never use long paragraphs.> \n- Never use unnecessary hashtags on the image.> \n> \nTYPOGRAPHY:> \n- Use professional sans-serif fonts only.> \n- Preferred headline font: Montserrat ExtraBold.> \n- Preferred secondary font: Inter Medium/SemiBold.> \n- Use uppercase for category labels.> \n- Use sentence case or uppercase for headlines depending on the design.> \n- Maintain consistent typography across all Global Pulse News posts.> \n> \nFINAL QUALITY:> \n- The image must look like a professional international news organization's social-media graphic.> \n- Clean composition.> \n- Strong visual hierarchy.> \n- Excellent mobile readability.> \n- High contrast.> \n- No unnecessary decorative elements.> \n- No excessive icons or emojis.> \n- No misleading visual elements.> \n- No fabricated information.> \n- The photograph and headline must accurately represent the news story.",
