    "Here are practical ways to boost reach and engagement on your Facebook page:\n\n---\n\n## 1. Hook in the first line\nFacebook truncates posts after ~3 lines before \"See More\". The first sentence must stop the scroll. Instead of starting with context, lead with the most shocking/interesting fact.\n\n**Current pattern:** \"In a significant development, [country] has announced...\"\n**Better:** \"Germany just banned its largest far-right party. Here's what that means for Europe. 🧵\"\n\n---\n\n## 2. Post format — use short paragraphs\nWalls of text get skipped. Break your generated posts into 2-3 line chunks with line breaks between them. Add a blank line between each thought. Facebook rewards posts people actually read to the end (dwell time).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Emojis as visual anchors\nUse 1-2 emojis per paragraph as bullet replacements — not decoration. Each category should have a consistent emoji identity:\n- 🔴 Breaking, ⚔️ War, 🌍 World, 💼 Business, 📱 Tech, 🌿 Climate, etc.\n\n---\n\n## 4. End with a question\nPosts that get comments rank much higher. The last line of every post should ask the audience something direct:\n\n\"What do you think — is this the right move? Drop your opinion below 👇\"\n\n---\n\n## 5. Hashtags — fewer is more\n3-5 highly relevant hashtags outperform 15 generic ones. Facebook's algorithm treats hashtag spam as low-quality. Stick to the most specific ones per story.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Post timing\nPeak Facebook engagement windows (general):\n- **7–9 AM** local time (morning scroll)\n- **12–2 PM** (lunch break)\n- **7–10 PM** (evening)\n\nAvoid posting at 3–6 AM — your posts age before your audience wakes up.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Image quality matters for reach\nFacebook gives organic reach boost to posts with images that get saved/shared. Your current 1200×1500 format is good. Make sure:\n- Headline text is readable on mobile (your current 58–80px is solid)\n- Don't put critical text in the bottom 20% (Facebook sometimes crops previews)\n\n---\n\n## 8. Consistency over volume\nPosting 3–5 times/day consistently beats posting 14 at once. Facebook penalizes burst posting — it looks like spam to the algorithm. Space posts at least 1–2 hours apart.\n\n---\n\n## What I can improve in the agent right now:\n\n| Improvement | Effort |\n|---|---|\n| Add a question at the end of every generated post | Small — update the LLM prompt in `generator.py` |\n| Reduce hashtags to 5 max | Small — update `content_validator.py` |\n| Enforce short paragraphs (line breaks every 2-3 lines) | Small — post-processing in `generator.py` |\n| Add category emoji to opening line | Small — `generator.py` |\n| Scheduled posting at peak hours | Medium — add a scheduler to `agent.py` |\n\nWant me to implement any or all of these?\n[Tool uses: none]",
