    "The scoring engine is good but I'd add these improvements:\n\n**1. Corroboration bonus in Breaking/Urgency — not just Credibility**\nA breaking story confirmed by 3+ sources should score higher than one from a single source. Right now corroboration only affects credibility. It should also boost urgency.\n\n**2. Category-aware scoring**\nA \"war\" story scoring 55 should still beat a \"trending\" story scoring 70. Category weight should apply a multiplier, not just keywords. A 🔴 breaking/war/crime story hitting HOLD because it lacks keywords is an editorial mistake.\n\n**3. Penalty for opinion/analysis pieces that slip through**\nWords like \"opinion\", \"why X matters\", \"what we know\", \"explainer\", \"analysis\" should reduce news value — they're commentary, not news.\n\n**4. Recency of the *event*, not just the article**\nAn article published 1 hour ago about something that happened 3 days ago shouldn't score 10 on freshness. If the summary contains phrases like \"last week\", \"days ago\", \"earlier this month\" — freshness should be penalized.\n\n**5. Geographic reach signal**\nA story affecting 1 country scores lower than one affecting multiple nations. Words like \"global\", \"worldwide\", \"international\", \"UN\", \"NATO\", \"G7\", \"multiple countries\" → audience interest bonus.\n\n**6. Engagement prediction from title structure**\nTitles phrased as questions (\"Is X happening?\"), with numbers (\"5 dead\", \"100,000 affected\"), or with named individuals (proper nouns) consistently get more Facebook engagement. These should get an audience interest boost.\n\n**7. Soft floor for HOLD tier — don't auto-reject, just delay**\nRight now HOLD (60–69) does nothing different from PUBLISH in the queue logic. The queue should treat HOLD stories as fillers — only publish them if no PUBLISH/HIGH/PRIORITY story is available in that window.\n\n---\n\nHere's my recommended revised breakdown:\n\n```\nNEWS VALUE              30 pts  (same — your instinct is right)